<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bergistani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.) · capital Bergium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Iberian people of the Catalan pre-Pyrenees whose repeated revolts against Cato in 195 BCE ended in their enslavement.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bergistani lived in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llobregat">Llobregat</a> valley of central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a>, a region still called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergueda">Berguedà</a> after them. They were an Iberian-speaking hill people whose main stronghold was the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergium">Bergium</a>, perhaps near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berga">Berga</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known about their society beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy's</a> narrative. They lived from mixed farming and herding in a mountainous district and defended themselves from fortified hilltops.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 195 BCE they rose twice against the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato</a>. After the second revolt he took their strongholds and sold the inhabitants into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergium">Bergium</a> itself fell when its chief, who said brigands had seized it, helped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> inside. The territory was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:6.07%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 195 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bergium</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bergistanians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=bergistani" aria-label="Bergistani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4591 757 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bergistani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4911 1013h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4911 1013h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-348&amp;focus=bergistani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
